Z||000000||Gokart||01-05-2000||09:16 PM||||My temp gauge isn't working right. I had a brand new high temp thermostat and just bought another but still hardly budges over the 100 mark. Cobra told me which one when he was over here last Teusday, but he showed me so many things I forget? DUH! I know I shouldn't complain cause overheating is more likely, but I don't know if it's the engine running cold which I'm sure could be dangerous in the months ahead. TIA.||||reg||5
Z||000001||AL||01-05-2000||09:41 PM||||gokart, the sensor for the gauge is the one under the valve cover next to the distributor, it has two wires going to the sensor, change that, and it should work perfectly.i recommend you buy it at the dealer cause the aftermarket one's sometimes don't work right.good luck, AL||||reg||1
